cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Kiln in your research, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "Kiln: WebGPU-native out-of-core volume rendering"
abstract: >-
  Kiln is a WebGPU-native, out-of-core volume renderer for large volumetric
  datasets. It streams multiscale OME-Zarr (NGFF v0.4/v0.5) and a sharded
  binary format over HTTP into a bounded GPU residency cache using
  virtual-texture indirection, and renders them in the browser with
  compute-shader ray marching (direct volume rendering, maximum intensity
  projection, isosurface and slice views) at interactive frame rates.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Martin
    family-names: Panknin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1257-1705"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MPanknin/kiln-render"
url: "https://kilnrender.com"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-09-28"
keywords:
  - WebGPU
  - volume rendering
  - out-of-core rendering
  - virtual texturing
  - OME-Zarr
  - NGFF
  - Zarr
  - scientific visualization
  - microscopy
  - bioimaging
